user_prompt:
Build the reconciliation report from recon_adjudication_package.adjudicated_items, optionally enriching evidence with chart_canonical_package excerpts, governed by packaging_options and scoring_policy.

Scoring (deterministic; all scores are 0-100 integers, clamped to that range):
- recon_match_rate_pct = exact_match_count / total_unique_line_keys (from the upstream S12 diff summary), expressed as an integer percentage.
- recon_denial_risk_score_pct: start at 0 and add, for each item: DENIAL_RISK impact_class with an unresolved disposition +10; modifier in {QW,25,59,95} with a needs-review disposition +15; INSUFFICIENT_DOC disposition +10. Clamp 0-100.
- recon_variance_severity_score_pct: start at 0 and add, for each item: UNDERBILL or OVERBILL high severity +10; BOTH_INCORRECT +20; root_cause_tag AI_RULE_LOGIC_ERROR or PAYER_PROFILE_MISMATCH +10. Clamp 0-100. These scores measure reconciliation quality, not absolute coding accuracy. Weight the overall narrative emphasis using scoring_policy's match_rate_weight / denial_risk_weight / documentation_ambiguity_weight.

Report generation logic (deterministic):
- Prioritize issues by: (1) impact_class priority DENIAL_RISK > OVERBILL > UNDERBILL > QUALITY_GAP > NEUTRAL; (2) disposition priority INSUFFICIENT_DOC / NEEDS_REVIEW first; (3) presence of contra evidence. Include at most packaging_options.max_top_issues items in top_issues, ordered per packaging_options.grouping_strategy.
- Group findings into: Modifiers, Units, Missing/Extra Billable Lines, Quality Reporting, Policy/Profile Issues, Crosswalk/Mapping Gaps. Only include items present in recon_adjudication_package.
- Each top_issues card must contain: title, what AI vs Human did, disposition, why it matters (risk), evidence refs (and optional snippets), and recommended action.

Provider query packet (only if packaging_options.include_provider_query_packet=true): generate a query item only when disposition is INSUFFICIENT_DOC, or root cause is AMBIGUOUS_DOCUMENTATION, or a deterministic policy requirement cannot be confirmed (rare). Each query includes query_id, issue_summary, non_leading_questions[] (max 3), allowed_answer_formats[], and evidence_refs[]. Provider queries must never contain CPT/HCPCS codes or patterns.

Engineering tickets (only if packaging_options.include_engineering_tickets=true): emit structured tasks — CROSSWALK_UPDATE (missing mapping key, example vaccine/lab string, desired output type), PROFILE_FIX (payer profile mismatch, e.g. specimen allow/deny or QW policy), PIPELINE_FIX (extraction miss patterns or rule logic issues).

Validations: scores are integers 0-100; provider query packet contains no CPT/HCPCS patterns; evidence refs must exist in chart_canonical_package if snippets are included; top_issues length <= packaging_options.max_top_issues; grouped_findings only includes items present in the adjudication package.

